{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs4P1cyrLS4NnFtm2zgS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The root cause was mutable default arguments in `inv/warehouse.py`. Python evaluates a default once, at function definition, so every `Warehouse` and every `restock` call shared the same objects:\n\n- `Warehouse.__init__(self, name, stock={}, history=[])`: all warehouses shared one `stock` dict and one `history` list. That's why a second warehouse showed the first one's stock.\n- `restock(..., tags=[])`: the shared `tags` list was stored on each new `Item`, so items from different calls could share and mutate one list.\n\n**The fix** (`inv/warehouse.py`):\n- `stock` and `history` now default to `None`, and `__init__` creates a fresh `{}` or `[]` per instance when no value is passed.\n- `tags` defaults to `None`. `restock` stores `list(tags or [])`, so each new `Item` gets its own list and doesn't alias the caller's list either.\n\nI did not change `tests/test_inv.py`.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `python -m pytest -q` in the case directory: `1 passed`.\n- A direct check confirmed that two warehouses have separate `stock` and `history` objects, and that a restock on one doesn't affect the other. It also confirmed that item tags are not shared with the caller's list.\n- I removed the `__pycache__` and `.pytest_cache` directories my runs created. The only change in the working tree is `inv/warehouse.py`.\n\nI didn't commit. The change is uncommitted in the working tree, so you can review it first. I didn't run any other test suite because the case directory contains only the one test file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1541,"cache_read_input_tokens":34634,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1541},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"56a26848-0321-4901-af74-98406279e843","uuid":"c602f9ac-ecf8-497c-bad9-3017faab8464","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:29:29.670Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs4P1MrRcMfLRHSnwLhX"}
